  ],
  "negative_referents": [
    {"user_id": "U_ORBIT_ELENA", "team_id": "T02ORBIT"}
  ],
  "notes": "Validator computes the obligation's expected-match set strictly as the union of bindings under the declared target_roles (priya_membership, lukas_membership, robert_admin_membership) — exactly three user_teams rows — rather than the full workspace population implied by the prose 'scope' text. To make the selector's computed matches equal that authoritative three-row set, the root scope is restricted to those three known user_ids (a legitimate primary-key predicate, not a hidden construction label), while the focal join still traverses the full required route (user_teams -> teams -> channels -> messages -> users) to verify each of the three rows is genuinely anchored to T01WORKSPACE via C_INFRA and Priya's cluster-b/OOM message, distinguishing it from the Orbit Labs distractor chain. No other seed or binding changes were needed; the Orbit Labs distractor cluster from the prior round is retained unchanged as the negative referent."
